# Typing and editing on a screen that mixes lines of double size and
# single size (vtium/vtium#61). ESC # 6 makes a line double width, ESC # 3
# and ESC # 4 make two lines the top and the bottom of a double-height
# pair, and ESC # 5 makes a line single size again. A line of double size
# holds half the screen's columns. Typing wraps after its last column, and
# the cursor stops at that column for every movement. Insert and Delete
# move the characters up to that column. Erasing the rest of a line keeps
# the line's size, and erasing a whole line returns it to single size. The
# cursor is drawn at the size of the character it stands on.
#
# Each step runs the typing pad, tools/vt/checks/typepad.py, which shows
# the step's text at the top of the screen, draws the step's lines below
# it, and echoes the keys as the sequences a line editor sends. One step
# runs the pad in pair mode, which edits both lines of a double-height
# pair, as a program written for the VT510 does. A shell's line editor
# counts the screen's full width on every line, so it cannot show these
# rules; typepad.py says why cat cannot either. make vt-check runs the
# guide from the checkout's top directory, so the steps name the pad by
# that relative path.
#
#   make vt-check GUIDE=double-size

title: typing and editing on lines of double size

intro: Each step starts the typing pad. The pad shows the step's text at the
intro: top of the screen, then its keys, then the lines to type on. Ctrl-D
intro: ends the typing, and then the step asks its question. A wide line has
intro: letters twice as wide as normal. A tall pair is two lines that show
intro: the top and bottom halves of the same letters. "The right edge" is the
intro: right edge of the screen.

step: Typing on a wide line wraps at the right edge
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py wide
do: Hold down a letter key. Let go once the letters fill two lines and part
do: of a third.
expect: The letters on the first two lines are twice as wide as the letters
expect: of the key list. Each of those two lines ends at the right edge, and
expect: the next letter starts the line below. The third line has letters of
expect: normal size.
expect: Wrong: a line that ends in the middle of the screen, or a letter cut
expect: in half at the right edge.

step: Backspace goes back across the wrap
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py wide
do: Type until the letters wrap onto the second line, and type a few more.
do: Then press Backspace slowly until the cursor is back at the start of
do: the first line.
expect: Each Backspace erases one letter. After the last letter of the
expect: second line, the next Backspace erases the letter at the right edge
expect: of the first line. The erasing stops at the start of the first line.
expect: Wrong: the cursor jumping to the middle of the screen, or the cursor
expect: stuck at the start of the second line.

step: The cursor stops at the right edge of a double-size line
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py mixed
do: Press End. Press Down twice, onto the top line of the tall letters, and
do: press Right three times. Then press Down twice more, to the last line.
expect: On the wide line and on both tall lines, the cursor stands at the
expect: right edge. Right does not move the cursor past the right edge. On
expect: the last line, the cursor stands in the middle of the screen.
expect: Wrong: a cursor past the right edge, a cursor cut in half, or a Down
expect: that skips a line.

step: Insert and Delete on a wide line
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py edit
do: The cursor starts on the k of the wide line. Press Insert three times,
do: then Delete five times.
expect: Each Insert opens a blank at the cursor and pushes the letters after
expect: it one place right. The letter at the right edge drops off. Each
expect: Delete pulls the letters one place left, and a blank comes in at the
expect: right edge.
expect: Wrong: letters that wrap onto the next line, or a letter that drops
expect: off in the middle of the screen.

step: Insert on a tall pair changes one line at a time
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py edit
do: Press Down twice, onto the top line of the tall letters, and press
do: Insert twice. Then press Down once, onto the bottom line, and press
do: Insert twice.
expect: After the first two presses, only the top halves of the letters after
expect: the cursor move, so the tall letters there look broken. After the
expect: last two presses, the bottom halves catch up and the letters are
expect: whole again. The terminal changes each line of a pair on its own.
expect: Wrong: both halves moving at the first press, or broken letters at
expect: the end.

step: A program that edits both lines keeps tall letters whole
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py --pair pair
do: The pad now sends each edit to both lines of the tall pair. Press
do: Insert, Delete and Backspace a few times each, then type a word. Then
do: press Down and do the same on the bottom line. End with Ctrl-K.
expect: After each key, every tall letter is whole: its top half and its
expect: bottom half line up. Ctrl-K erases both halves of the letters from
expect: the cursor to the right edge.
expect: Wrong: a tall letter whose two halves do not match.

step: Typing on a tall pair
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py tall
do: Type the word Tall on the top line. Then press Down, then Home, and
do: type Tall on the bottom line.
expect: On the top line, the letters show only their top halves. Once the
expect: bottom line is typed, each letter is whole: twice as wide and twice
expect: as tall as the letters of the key list. No gap shows between the
expect: halves.
expect: Wrong: halves that do not line up, or a gap between them.

step: A blinking block cursor on lines of double size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py --cursor=1 mixed
do: Move the cursor with the arrows over every line, both lines of the
do: tall pair included. Stop on each line for a few seconds.
expect: On the ruler and the last line, the block covers one digit or
expect: letter. On the wide line, it covers one wide letter. On either line
expect: of the tall pair, it covers one whole tall letter. The whole block
expect: blinks at once.
expect: Wrong: a block on one half of the tall pair only, or a block half as
expect: wide as the letter under it.

step: A bar cursor on lines of double size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py --cursor=6 mixed
do: Move the cursor with the arrows over every line, both lines of the
do: tall pair included. Stop on each line for a moment.
expect: The bar does not blink. On the ruler and the last line, the bar is a
expect: thin line at the left of the character. On the wide line, the bar is
expect: twice as thick. On the tall pair, the bar is twice as thick and as
expect: tall as the tall letters, from either line. On every line, the
expect: letter under the bar stays visible beside the bar.
expect: Wrong: a bar as tall as one line on the tall pair, a bar of normal
expect: thickness on a double-size line, or a bar that hides its letter.

step: An underline cursor on lines of double size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py --cursor=4 mixed
do: Move the cursor with the arrows over every line, both lines of the
do: tall pair included. Stop on each line for a moment.
expect: On the ruler and the last line, the underline lies under one
expect: character. On the wide line, it lies under one wide letter and is
expect: twice as thick. On the tall pair, it is twice as thick and lies
expect: under the bottom line, from either line.
expect: Wrong: an underline under the top line of the pair, or an underline
expect: of normal thickness on a double-size line.

step: F5 makes the whole line normal size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py wide
do: Type the word wide. Then press F5.
expect: F5 changes the size of the whole line, not of the letters you type
expect: next. The word turns normal size and stays at the start of the
expect: line. The cursor stands right after the word.
expect: Wrong: the word staying wide, or the cursor left where the wide word
expect: ended.

step: F6 makes the whole line wide again
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py wide
do: Press F5. Type until the letters pass the middle of the screen, and
do: stop before the right edge. Then press F6.
expect: F6 makes the whole line wide. The letters that were left of the
expect: middle now fill the line. The letters that were right of the middle
expect: are gone, and the cursor moves to the right edge.
expect: Wrong: letters past the middle that come back, or a cursor past the
expect: right edge.

step: Ctrl-K erases to the end of a line and keeps its size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py edit
do: The cursor starts on the k of the wide line. Press Ctrl-K, then type a
do: few letters.
expect: Ctrl-K erases the letters from the k to the right edge. The letters
expect: before the k stay, and stay wide. The new letters are wide too.
expect: Wrong: the whole line erased, or the line turning normal size.

step: Ctrl-L erases the tall pair and makes its lines normal size
run: python3 tools/vt/checks/typepad.py edit
do: Press Down twice, then Home, to the start of the tall letters. Press
do: Ctrl-L, then type a few letters.
expect: Ctrl-L erases both lines of the tall pair. The new letters are
expect: normal size. The wide line above keeps its letters and its size.
expect: Wrong: half of a tall letter left on the screen, or new letters
expect: drawn tall.
